# layer-inversion ratchet (web/css/README.md, "The inversion check").
#
# One line per file pair, `<lower> > <higher> <count>`: the number of rules in
# the lower layer's sheet that are more specific than a rule in the higher
# layer's sheet they compete with, and so lose to it under the @layers — dead
# overrides. It is empty: scripts/lint-css-arch fails when a count rises, when a pair
# appears that is not listed, and when a count falls without this file being
# lowered to match — so the numbers only come down. To see one pair:
#
#   node scripts/lint-css-arch --inversions <lower> <higher>
#
# This is the only counted debt in the CSS lint. Every other check has no
# exceptions.
